# Release Workflow

- Maintain separate update paths for `experimental` (testing), `paid` (paid-feature testing), and `main` (stable user path).
- Track one active working branch at a time, and default all routine commits/pushes to that active branch.
- Before each push, resolve the target branch using branch memory:
  1) If the user explicitly requests a branch switch in this chat, use that branch and set it as active.
  2) Otherwise, reuse the branch used by the last successful push in this chat session.
  3) If there is no prior push in this chat session, use the current configured default active branch.
- Treat `paid` as the active branch until the user explicitly instructs a branch switch.
- After a user requests a branch switch, assume all future routine commits/pushes go to the newly selected branch until instructed otherwise.
- Push to `main` only when explicitly instructed.
- When promoting changes between branches, carry over only intended updates and preserve separation between update paths.
- **Bug fixes** in this repository: when you finish a fix, **commit and push to `origin/experimental`** with a clear message (unless the user directs another branch in the same thread). Do not leave bugfix changes uncommitted at the end of the turn if the user expects them merged via CI.
- After a **successful `git push` to `origin/experimental`** for this repo, start the deferred CI watcher (non-blocking). From repo root use **`-WorkingDirectory`** and **`-WindowStyle Hidden`** so no PowerShell window flashes, e.g. `Start-Process powershell.exe -WindowStyle Hidden -WorkingDirectory (Get-Location).Path -ArgumentList '-NoProfile','-ExecutionPolicy','Bypass','-WindowStyle','Hidden','-File',(Join-Path (Get-Location).Path 'tools\defer-experimental-ci-watch.ps1')` — waits **6 minutes**, then runs `tools/watch-experimental-ci-and-install.ps1` (needs **GitHub CLI** `gh` + auth). On failure it logs to **`%TEMP%\zubcut-ci-watch.log`** and opens it in Notepad. Skip if the user asked not to run installers or the push was not to `experimental`.
